      "title": "Countable, uncountable, some and any",
      "subtitle": "Sustantivos contables e incontables con some / any",
      "goals": [
        "Distinguir sustantivos **contables** e **incontables**.",
        "Usar **some** en afirmativas y **any** en negativas y preguntas.",
        "Ofrecer y pedir con *Would you like some…?*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "¿Se puede contar?",
      "table": {
        "head": ["", "Contables", "Incontables"],
        "rows": [
          ["Ejemplos", "apple, chair, student, egg", "water, rice, money, bread, information, homework"],
          ["Singular", "**an** apple", "— (no llevan *a / an*)"],
          ["Plural", "apple**s**", "— (no tienen plural)"],
          ["Verbo", "There **are** some apples.", "There **is** some water."]
        ]
      },
      "watch": "Algunos son incontables en inglés pero no en español: **information, advice, homework, furniture, news, money**. Se dice *some information*, nunca *informations*."
